dialogue cohesion_generic_support_any
title: Small mercies
trigger: Cohesion role:Support any level=4
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker with $with
speaker hero $hero

node open commander
  The Support has been up before everyone again: boots oiled, water skins filled, a spare strap laid by every bedroll. Tonight one hero is still awake to catch the Support at it.
  -> caught

node caught hero
  So it's you. Every morning my gear's better than I left it. I thought the caravan had a ghost.
  -> ghost

node ghost with
  A ghost would do it better. I just don't sleep much. And a loose strap in a fight is worse than any blade.
  -> thanks

node thanks hero
  Nobody thanks you for it. I've never heard anyone say a word. Commander, have you?
  * I've seen it. I should have said so sooner. Thank you, both of you, for noticing. -> seen
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 8
  * Then say it now. It means more from the one whose straps got fixed. -> now
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 10
  * The Support doesn't do it for thanks. Leave it be. -> leave
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -3

node seen with
  Noticing's plenty. More than plenty. I'd go on doing it either way.
  -> fight

node now hero
  Thank you, then. For the straps, and the boots, and whatever else I never caught.
  -> fight

node leave hero
  Maybe not. But it should still be said.
  -> fight

node fight with
  You want to know the truth? I watch you in a fight, every time. When you stumble, I'm already moving. It's easier when I know someone's watching back.
  -> back

node back hero
  Then I'll watch back. Every fight. And some mornings, I'll be up first.
  * Up first together. Two pairs of hands, half the time. -> together
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 9
  * Watch back, yes. But let the Support sleep in once in a while. -> sleep
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero 7
  * Your own gear is your own work. Look to that first. -> own
    do: AddCohesion $with $hero -2

node together with
  Half the time. I don't know what I'll do with the other half. Sleep, maybe.
  -> close

node sleep with
  Sleep in. That'd be something. I'll try it once and see if the caravan falls apart.
  -> close

node own hero
  My own gear. Fine. But I'm still saying thank you.
  -> close

node close commander
  Before dawn, two figures move between the bedrolls with oil and spare straps, whispering, and the work is done in half the time.
